# React Frontend Rules

- Build small, reusable components with a single responsibility.
- Keep component APIs explicit and typed; avoid large ambiguous prop objects.
- Prefer composition over deep prop drilling and overgrown component files.
- Keep state as local as possible; lift only when multiple siblings need shared state.
- Extract repeated UI logic into custom hooks when it appears in multiple components.
- Keep presentational components focused on rendering and interaction, not data orchestration.

## Example
```tsx
type SubmitButtonProps = {
  isLoading: boolean;
  onClick: () => void;
};
```
